Spec: SpecDD Convergence Augmentation

Purpose:
  Add SpecDD actual-change verification to `speckit.converge` without replacing upstream feature convergence semantics.

Owns:
  ./converge.md

References:
  ../../specdd/commands/verify.sdd
  ../../specdd/commands/authorize.sdd

Must:
  Convergence verifies actual changes against the immutable authorization snapshot before reporting a clean result.
  Feature gaps remain distinct from deterministic SpecDD system and authority findings.
  Convergence recognizes `SPECDD_VIOLATION`, `SPECDD_DRIFT`, `MISSING_SPEC_EVOLUTION`, and `AUTHORITY_VIOLATION`.
  Blocking SpecDD authority or lint findings prevent a clean converged result.
  Current feature Change Boundary state does not replace authorization evidence from before implementation.
  Changed `.sdd` files never retroactively authorize implementation writes from the same operation.

Done when:
  The composed convergence command retains upstream append-only behavior and includes SpecDD verification findings against historical authorization evidence.
